                <pb facs="0388" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862t.01/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-24T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>595. Your 790, March 22, 8 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department in general approves statement of Rhineland High Commissioners but
                    feels that in emergency these interned troops <pb facs="0389" n="299"
                        xml:id="pg299"/> might properly be used on request of German Government for
                    suppression of disorders in Ruhr district or elsewhere in accord with
                    Department’s 575, March 22, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
